{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4707",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufb1 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which in turn participate in the Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity, ultimately leading to Ndufb1 being a participant in this process. This indicates that Metformin may influence Ndufb1 through a mechanism involving the regulation of Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity. The high scores across the three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, with Metformin potentially modulating Ndufb1 via a pathway that involves the regulation of the Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity. The overlapping roles of Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 in this pathway highlight the importance of these subunits in the overall function of Nadh Dehydrogenase, and thus, Metformin's interaction with them may have a broader impact on Ndufb1's activity.",
